---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
    title="Fetch for Chrome privacy policy — Erik Role"
    description="Fetch for Chrome does not collect, store or send any data."
    canonicalUrl="https://erikrole.com/fetch/privacy"
>
    <main class="policy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Fetch for Chrome</p>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Updated November 6, 2026</p>

        <p>
            Fetch for Chrome does not collect, store or send any data. It has no accounts, no
            analytics and no servers.
        </p>
        <p>
            When you choose Save, the extension passes the address of the current page, or the
            link you right-clicked, to the Fetch app on your own Mac using a <code>fetch://</code>
            link. That hand-off stays on your computer. The extension does not send it anywhere
            else.
        </p>
        <p>
            The extension asks for two permissions. <strong>contextMenus</strong> adds the
            right-click items. <strong>activeTab</strong> reads the current tab's address and title
            when you click the toolbar button or press the shortcut.
        </p>
        <p>
            What the Fetch app itself does is covered by its own settings and notes.
        </p>
        <p>
            Questions: <a href="mailto:erikrole@gmail.com">erikrole@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    .policy {
        width: min(100% - 2 * var(--gutter), 42rem);
        margin-inline: auto;
        padding-block: 6rem 4rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; font-size: .8rem; opacity: .7; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
    h1 { font-family: var(--font-display, inherit); font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
    .updated { opacity: .7; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
    p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
</style>
